                                "sense_id": "8e279c17-afd6-3562-8e67-bffc381e5bb1",
                                "text": "You then shall for my fake this sheephook keep,\nAdorn'd with Brass[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e3e427a-7bae-4d69-a6fb-6e270e8bb30f",
                                "sense_id": "8e279c17-afd6-3562-8e67-bffc381e5bb1",
                                "text": "O'er both their marks it flew; till fiercely flung From Polypoetes' arm the discus sung: Far as a swain his whirling sheephook throws, That distant falls among the grazing cows, So past them all the rapid circle flies: His friends, while loud applauses shake the skies, With force conjoin'd heave off the weighty prize."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "185f75a5-d7ff-4ce5-9a4a-8c170bf88b23",
                                "sense_id": "8e279c17-afd6-3562-8e67-bffc381e5bb1",
                                "text": "For the shepherd of that unhappy sheepfold also had climbed up some other way before he knew how to hold a sheephook, till, week after week, the hungry sheep looked up and were not fed."
                            }
                        ]
